Do not link the etcd runit service in the no-DCS fallback: the embedded etcd
that upstream bundles for its demo mode (v3.3.27, end of life) is not shipped
in this image. The 127.0.0.1:2379 config is kept so an etcd sidecar sharing
the network namespace still works.
Upstream source: https://github.com/zalando/spilo/blob/4.1-p2/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py
diff --git a/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py b/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py
index 61f00ac..4412af6 100755
--- a/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py
+++ b/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py
@@ -1141,7 +1141,8 @@ def main():
     config = deep_update(user_config_copy, config)
 
     if provider == PROVIDER_LOCAL and not any(1 for key in config.keys() if key in PATRONI_DCS):
-        link_runit_service(placeholders, 'etcd')
+        logging.warning('No DCS configured (set ETCD_HOSTS, DCS_ENABLE_KUBERNETES_API, or SPILO_CONFIGURATION); '
+                        'expecting etcd on 127.0.0.1:2379')
         config['etcd'] = {'host': '127.0.0.1:2379'}
 
     pgdata = config['postgresql']['data_dir']
